/// How a bulk accessory is allocated against the shared pool.
/// SHIPS_WITH: the parent "ships with" N of this bulk asset; the N are drawn
///   from the live pool at prep/checkout (a normal booking) — availability is
///   computed live, the pool is NOT decremented at attach time.
/// DEDICATED: the N are permanently pulled out of the shared pool at attach
///   time (kit-style availableQuantity decrement) and restored on detach/remove.
enum AccessoryAllocationMode {
  SHIPS_WITH
  DEDICATED
}

/// A bulk asset attached as a permanent accessory to a parent serialised asset
/// (e.g. "this light ships with 2 clamps"). Mirrors KitBulkItem.
/// A bulk asset declared as a default accessory at the Model level —
/// "every asset of this model ships with N of this bulk asset". When any
/// asset of the model is added to a project, model-level bulk accessories
/// auto-expand as child lines alongside the asset's own accessories, deduped
/// by bulkAssetId (asset-level wins on conflict). Model-level accessories are
/// always SHIPS_WITH (drawn from the live pool at prep) — DEDICATED only
/// makes sense at the asset level (you can't permanently reserve N from the
/// pool against every asset of a model — that'd drain the whole shelf).
// ─── Location ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

