// ─── Project Line-Item Unit ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
// One physical unit assigned to an order line. Replaces the old "split a
// qty-N line into N qty-1 rows" mechanism: serialised assets get one row each
// (quantity 1), bulk assets get one row carrying a quantity. Per-unit deploy /
// return state lives here, not on the order line.
// See docs/designs/line-item-fulfillment-model.md.

/// Audit trail for the Phase 3.8 split-sibling collapse migration.
///
/// When the historic data has lines that splitLineItem fragmented into
/// per-asset siblings, the collapse migration merges them back onto one
/// canonical order line — moving each sibling's ProjectLineItemUnit, its
/// CheckRecord rows, and its ProjectService onto the
/// canonical, then deactivating the old row. This table records the
/// mapping so the merge can be audited and (if needed) reversed.
///
/// Permanent — never auto-cleaned. One row per merged (old) line item.
// ─── Project Category ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// ─── Category Slot ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Cross-type ordering for ProjectGroup + SubHireGroup within a ProjectCategory.
// Each slot points at exactly one group (XOR enforced by DB check constraint
// added in the migration SQL — Prisma doesn't support CHECK in schema.prisma).
// The slot's sortOrder is the canonical ordering for queries that need a
// unified group list per category.

// ─── Project Group ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// ─── Project Manager (join table) ───────────────────────────────────────────

// ─── Kit Revenue Allocation ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

// One row per MODEL in a kit — not per member asset. A kit's contents are
// KitSerializedItem (one row per asset) and KitBulkItem rows; hanging a percentage
// off those would make the same model appear N times as N percentages to keep in
// sync, and would break the allocation every time an asset is swapped. Model is
// also the grain ROI reports on, so this is the natural key.
//
// CONVEX-ONLY (Phase C): no Prisma row is ever written. The Convex
// `kitRevenueAllocations` doc is the sole source of truth; this model exists so
// scripts/generate-convex-schema.cjs reproduces the table.
//
// Percentages are advisory, not load-bearing: the allocation is applied only when
// the saved model set exactly covers the kit's CURRENT contents. Kit contents can
// change without ever touching this table (warehouse, CSV import), so the runtime
// falls through to the weight chain rather than trusting a stale split.
// ─── Project Model Revenue (rollup) ─────────────────────────────────────────

// Derived rollup: one row per (project, model), rebuilt wholesale by the same
// allocation pass that writes ProjectLineItem.allocatedRevenue. Pure cache — safe
// to delete and rebuild from line items at any time.
//
// It exists so the fleet ROI report reads "distinct models per project" instead of
// "every line item of every project", which does not fit in a Convex query's read
// budget. See the "Query cost" section of docs/revenue-allocation-design.md.
//
// CONVEX-ONLY (Phase C): no Prisma row is ever written.
// ─── Group Template ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// ─── Group Template Item ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

